Z||000003||Carrolles||12-09-1999||12:53 PM||||By looking pretty weak do you mean that the shaft is worn?  If not, simply disassemble the distributor and clean up the shaft with some steel wool and solvent.<P>I overhauled mine when I had the engine out.  It was in good shape but I polished the shaft anyway and installed new pick-up coil and cleaned the rust off the reluctor.<P>Don't forget to install a new o-ring before you reinstall.<P>If you use an electric drill to prime your new oil pump don't forget to place a stack of washers over the hole where the distributor enters the manifold to close up the hole or you will be swimming in oil.  It is amazing how much oil is pumped up the distributor drive shaft.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dogtired||12-09-1999||02:18 PM||||Just a little info! Pulled my distributor and the hex (oil pump drive) shaft came out with it. Which was OK. Sent the motor to machine shop for rebuild and they longblocked it, and also put a new hex shaft in it. So I stuck a socket on it and primed the oil pump. Put the rest of the motor back together, fired it up and had NO oil pressure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Panic time. Well I suspected the shaft was too short to fit up in the distributor properly, so I pulled it. The shafts were the same length but the new shaft was hex shaped its full length EXCEPT for about 3/4 inch about 3/4 inch from where it went into the distributor. Aparently only about 3/4 inch inside the distributor is hex shaped? The shaft fit right up inside the distributor to where the non-hex part of the shaft was where the hex part of the distributor drive was, therefore it just spun on the shaft. Thats the long story. The short story: Use only a shaft that is HEX shaped all the way up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> This is certainly a fool proof way to check your own blood pressure! Good Luck.||||reg||7
Z||000005||2FAST4U||12-10-1999||12:35 AM||||I just talked to MSD last week looking for a distributer for my car. The distributer they list in their catalog does not work with the stock ECU. They suggested a new OEM distributer (or rebuilt) with their Digital six controller and coil.||||reg||1
